warning[W0801]: `Gratuity` binds a new name here — it does not test the variant `Kind.Gratuity`
 --> mem:///main.lu:8:27
  |
1 | enum Kind { Drink, Food, Gratuity }
  |                          -------- `Gratuity` is declared here, in `Kind`
...
8 |     let a = pick(0) else |Gratuity| 7
  |                           ^^^^^^^^ a binding, not a test
  |
  = note: a `let`, `var`, `for` or `else |…|` pattern binds every value it meets, so a bare name
    there is a new binding even when it spells a variant. To test the value, `match` on it
    (`Kind.Gratuity => …`); to keep the binding, give it a name that spells no variant.
help: bind it under another name: `gratuity`
  |
8 |     let a = pick(0) else |gratuity| 7
  |
help: test the variant instead: `Kind.Gratuity`
  |
8 |     let a = pick(0) else |Kind.Gratuity| 7
  |
